  "details": "Currently, when Ambient Occlusion (AO) is included as part of a world’s post-processing, it often improves the overall look of the environment but can have a strong impact on avatars — especially on their eyes.\n\nThis sometimes causes avatars’ eyes to appear unnaturally dark or shaded. Because of this, there are even “AO canceller” contact lenses being sold to counteract the effect.\n\nWhile some worlds provide a switch to toggle AO, many do not.\n\nIt would be very helpful if users could adjust AO intensity — just like Bloom — directly from the settings.\n\nBeing able to reduce or disable AO without needing avatar-side workarounds would make the experience much more comfortable and visually consistent across different worlds.\n\nThank you.",
